   "id": "g_deploy",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "Deployment: one kernel, many khoras",
   "x": -100,
   "y": 318,
   "width": 2300,
   "height": 2630
  },
  {
   "id": "g_sources",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "Entity sources (one contract: capabilities, negotiate, execute, changes?, invoke?)",
   "x": -50,
   "y": 2430,
   "width": 2200,
   "height": 468,
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "g_kernel",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "Kernel",
   "x": -50,
   "y": 904,
   "width": 2200,
   "height": 1426,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "g_iface",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "Interface",
   "x": 380,
   "y": 388,
   "width": 1340,
   "height": 416,
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "g_principals",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "Principals and content",
   "x": -50,
   "y": -80,
   "width": 1770,
   "height": 338,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -760,
   "width": 1150,
   "height": 560,
   "text": "# khora: projected architecture\n\nThe runtime system as the ADRs currently project it (10.11.2026). Nothing is built yet; status per ADR: 0XX, 0XY, 0XZ, 0YA proposed; 0YB provisional.\n\n- One **deployment** runs one kernel and hosts many khoras. Khoras are scopes with a center, not separate stacks.\n- The **action log** is the source of truth for internal entities. Datastores, indexes, access labels, lenses and process state are projections of it.\n- Everything the kernel works with is itself an entity: kinds, claims, behaviors, scopes, grants, process definitions, subscriptions.\n- Domain systems install as content: kinds, behaviors, operations, controllers and processes.\n- **Open:** marks choices that are not made yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1200,
   "y": -760,
   "width": 560,
   "height": 560,
   "text": "## Flows (edge colors)\n- **Blue: read.** API → planner → claims → fragments to sources → batches → access filter → result with metadata.\n- **Orange: write.** API → action layer (rights, approval, budget) → operation → action appended to the log.\n- **Green: reactive.** Log → projections → subscriptions → live views, controllers, waiting processes.\n- **Purple: external.** Connectors sync outside content in as actions, and write back through an outbox.\n- **Grey: structure.** Uses, reads config from, hosted in."
  },
  {
   "id": "staging",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1810,
   "y": -760,
   "width": 700,
   "height": 560,
   "text": "## Staging (ADR-0YA d17)\n1. **MVP:** pure behaviors run in the kernel; operations are executed by principals (people, agents, services, controllers); the kernel is a data-and-log system.\n2. **Native:** khora's own runtime executes declarative operations, queries first, then writes. Controllers for them become an implementation detail.\n3. **Self-hosting:** the runtime is modeled data, produced and checked by its previous version. Only the firmware stays outside (PRD P1).\n\nInteroperability between deployments (right side) is PRD P1 and marked *interop: review* throughout."
  },
  {
   "id": "people",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## People\n- Work through representations, not raw entities.\n- Act as principals; every action records actor and on whose behalf.",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 208
  },
  {
   "id": "agents",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## AI agents\n- Consumers of the system, not its core.\n- Reach khora through the API (e.g. MCP).\n- Discover their tools from the operations granted in their scope.",
   "x": 430,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 208
  },
  {
   "id": "domain",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Domain systems (content)\n- Company brain, built-environment review, lifelong learning, application development, furniture workshop, nutrition.\n- Install as kinds, behaviors, operations, controllers, process definitions and lenses.\n- Never change the kernel.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 208
  },
  {
   "id": "api",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## khora API\n- `query(Query)`: reads, pinned to a frontier.\n- `invoke(operation, args)`: writes as governed actions.\n- `subscribe(Query)`: live results with a cursor.\n- One principal per call; scope is the context.",
   "x": 430,
   "y": 468,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 286
  },
  {
   "id": "views",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Representations\n- View = lens + cut + representation.\n- Canvas, reports, dashboards, compressed context for agents.\n- Collapsed scopes show aggregates; expanded ones their members.\n- Live by default: built on subscriptions.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 468,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 286
  },
  {
   "id": "ctx",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Context assembly\n- Scoped context for a task, entity or question.\n- Composed from views and queries under the caller's rights.\n- Serves agents and tutors in the domain systems.",
   "x": 1290,
   "y": 468,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 286
  },
  {
   "id": "qengine",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Query engine\n- Executes what sources could not: joins, Propagate, Aggregate, Not.\n- Propagate with named algebras: (or,and), (min,+), (max,×), (+,×), provenance.\n- Presets: BFS, shortest paths, PageRank, components, label and belief propagation.\n- Library: Leiden, embeddings, max flow, matching.\n- Calls only pure behaviors.\n- Generic loop until a pattern is recognized and specialized.",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 442
  },
  {
   "id": "planner",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Planner\n- Turns a Query into a plan over every entity source.\n- Looks up claims; negotiates pushdown per operation (exact / inexact / unsupported).\n- Inlines computed entities defined by a Query.\n- Pushes access labels down as filters; filters itself where a source can't.\n- Returns completeness, applied frontier, cost.\n- **Open:** DataFusion (Rust) / Calcite (JVM) / custom; Arrow batches; Substrait below.",
   "x": 430,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 442
  },
  {
   "id": "access",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Rights and access\n- Grants and agreements are entities in each scope's governance scope.\n- Rights: read, use, manage, grant, transfer, invoke.\n- Private by default; effective access = a grant chain.\n- Read access materialized as labels (a projection).\n- Restrictions follow derived data and effects.\n- Revocation cascades before any later read.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 442
  },
  {
   "id": "actionlayer",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Action layer\n- Every write is a governed action.\n- Checks rights: invoker ∩ operation grants; the invoke right.\n- Previews impact from declared writes and blast radius.\n- Requires approval for irreversible, external or high-impact operations.\n- Enforces declared writes; carries cascade budgets.\n- Dispatches to the source or runtime that claims the operation.",
   "x": 1290,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 442
  },
  {
   "id": "behavior",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Behavior runtime\n- Behaviors are entities, versioned by content hash.\n- Pure behaviors run in the kernel: computed attributes, rule checks, collapsed representations, Propagate updates.\n- Operations are run by principals in the MVP; natively later.\n- **Open:** language: declarative core + sandboxed opaque steps (e.g. WASM).",
   "x": 1720,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 442
  },
  {
   "id": "firmware",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Firmware\n- Boots the kernel from data.\n- Holds only the kernel schema and the location of the schema store.\n- Everything above it is data (PRD P1 self-containment).",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 390
  },
  {
   "id": "schema",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Schema store and catalog\n- Pinned store, itself an entity source.\n- Kinds (upper ontology + domain schemas as data).\n- Claims: which source holds which kinds, attributes, relations, capabilities and operations.\n- Versioned by log position.\n- Planner keeps it in memory.\n- **Open:** upper ontology choice.",
   "x": 430,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 390
  },
  {
   "id": "projector",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Projection engine\n- Folds the log into projections: datastores, indexes, access labels, scope memberships, lenses, process state.\n- Each projection reports the frontier it has applied.\n- Advances in dependency order: labels before streams.\n- Materialized where reads must be fast, on demand otherwise.\n- Snapshots = projections checkpointed at a frontier.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 390
  },
  {
   "id": "log",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Action log\n- Append-only, total order per log; at least one log per deployment.\n- Action = invocation + outcome + invertible deltas (attribute, relation, membership).\n- Content-hashed; causes form a causal graph; rejected attempts kept.\n- Frontier = one position per log; causally closed.\n- **Open:** log store (Redpanda/Kafka, NATS JetStream, embedded on object storage); partitioning.",
   "x": 1290,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 390
  },
  {
   "id": "controllers",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Controller host\n- Controllers are principals that react to subscriptions and invoke operations under a standing grant.\n- One execution home per controller (lease).\n- Record cause and frontier for every reaction; budgets stop cascades.\n- Run sync, housekeeping (lenses, labels, revocation, orphan decay) and domain automation.",
   "x": 1720,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 390
  },
  {
   "id": "subs",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Subscription service\n- Subscription = Query + cursor; the cursor is an entity.\n- At-least-once delivery; handlers idempotent by action id.\n- Incremental view maintenance by algebra: rings fully, semirings by counting or re-derivation, non-monotone by stratum.\n- Timers for thresholds; decay computed at read time.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 1916,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 364
  },
  {
   "id": "process",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Process runtime\n- Durable execution on the log: each step logs start, then completion or failure.\n- State = fold of the instance's own actions.\n- Waits (timers, approvals, human steps) are actions; nothing is held while waiting.\n- Pinned to its definition's version; sagas for failure.\n- **Open:** process language and engine.",
   "x": 1720,
   "y": 1916,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 364
  },
  {
   "id": "stores",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Typed datastores\n- Several stores by data shape: graph, relational / columnar, time series, search and vector, spatial.\n- Entities are virtual: a billion rows are entities without a graph store.\n- Each implements EntitySource and declares capabilities (traversal, semantic search, valid time, spatial, change feeds…).\n- All are projections of the log.",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 2510,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 338
  },
  {
   "id": "content",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Content store and keys\n- Large payloads stored once, addressed by hash.\n- Encrypted per entity or holder.\n- Deleting a key shreds the content; the action skeleton stays for audit.\n- **Open:** key granularity.",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 2510,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 338
  },
  {
   "id": "connectors",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## External connectors\n- External entities are proxies: content stays in its source.\n- Sync is a controller; each sync is an action.\n- Write-back via outbox: intent → attempt → confirmation.\n- Rights mirror the source's; khora only narrows them.\n- Stale sources are marked, never silently served.",
   "x": 1290,
   "y": 2510,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 338
  },
  {
   "id": "computed",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Computed entities\n- Defined by a Query: inlined by the planner, like views.\n- Defined by a pure behavior or opaque process: executed whole.\n- Report the oldest frontier among their inputs.\n- Materialized results: who recomputes is open.",
   "x": 1720,
   "y": 2510,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 338
  },
  {
   "id": "ext",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## External systems\n- Files and object storage, SaaS tools, databases, APIs, design and authoring tools.\n- Remain systems of record for their content in the first releases.",
   "x": 1290,
   "y": 3128,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 130
  },
  {
   "id": "fed_id",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Identity\n- Immutable content: id = hash, the same everywhere.\n- Everything else: issuer + local id; principals have DIDs.\n- Real-world things carry external ids.\n- Uncertain matches: same-as with confidence.",
   "x": 2420,
   "y": 984,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 260
  },
  {
   "id": "fed_index",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Pointer index\n- Deployments publish the claims they choose to.\n- Lookups go through a distributed index of pointers, not content.\n- Unpublished data is reachable only through a grant.\n- **Open:** protocol (study Holochain, Solid).",
   "x": 2420,
   "y": 1294,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 286
  },
  {
   "id": "fed_logs",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Logs and replicas\n- Logs replicate by need, not by global consensus.\n- Frontiers span logs; results are partial until logs arrive.\n- Replicas are one entity; divergence is a perspective or a flagged conflict.\n- Controller leases across deployments: open.",
   "x": 2420,
   "y": 1630,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 286
  }
 ],
